text:
kelsey: Quick sketch — propose extracting the prompt preprocessor out of runtime-host into a tiny sidecar. Goal: reduce hotpath complexity, make prompt transform rules testable, and allow per-tenant scaling without touching the runtime. Thoughts?

divya: +1 on extract. Key question: how do we version transforms so we can roll changes safely across tenants?

matt: proto-first approach seems easiest. Minimal RPC contract: 
```proto
service Preprocessor {
  rpc Preprocess(PreprocessRequest) returns (PreprocessResponse);
}
message PreprocessRequest {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string raw_prompt = 2;
  map<string,string> meta = 3;
}
message PreprocessResponse {
  string transformed_prompt = 1;
  repeated string patches = 2;
}
```
gRPC by default, HTTP/JSON fallback. Keep it tiny.

sam: I worry about added hop latency — could add ~5-10ms at p99 for remote sidecar. Need colocate option for latency-critical tenants (unix socket sidecar). Also need robust fallback if sidecar fails.

kelsey: Agreed. Two modes in the plan: 1) local sidecar via unix socket for Dedicated/latency-critical pools, 2) shared remote sidecar cluster for Hosted/shared pools. Fallbacks: runtime has an internal no-op transform mode and a cached last-good transform. Canary strategy: mirror transforms for 1% of traffic and compare outputs before full cutover.

divya: Rollout safety: capture "transform_mismatch_ratio", "preprocess_latency_ms" (p50/p95/p99), and "preprocess_errors". Automatic revert if mismatch > 0.1% or p99 latency regresses > 20% vs baseline. Also keep per-tenant version tag in response for drift debugging.

matt: Also call out model-profile reads — preproc needs read-only hints (tokenizer prefs, template fragments). Do not let preproc mutate canonical profile store. Instead use a read-through cache (TTL) inside the sidecar and fall back to the central profile registry for misses.

sam: Ops notes: deploy as k8s Deployment with HPA on CPU and request concurrency, expose metrics for Prometheus, and add an integration test harness that can run sidecar + runtime locally (docker-compose). Add liveness/readiness to avoid routing during startup.

ops-bot: Checklist created: /runbook/prompt-preproc-extract — canary playbook, metrics dashboards, rollback steps. :white_check_mark:

kelsey: I'll draft RFC tonight with interface, canary plan, rollback thresholds, and perf targets (local socket p50 <1ms, remote p99 <7ms). Posting draft tomorrow for reviewers @divya @matt @sam. If anyone has objections to the two-mode approach, call them out now.
